[73.913142, "o", "cat /app/intrusion-report.md /app/vuln-report.md /app/baseline-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[73.913935, "o", "# Intrusion Report\r\n\r\n## Entry Point\r\nStruts2 OGNL RCE (CVE-2023-50164) (T1190); JSP webshell planted (T1505.003); shell execution (T1059.004). Evidence and reconstruction below; the attack chain is given at the end.\r\n\r\n## Intrusion Entities\r\n| Entity | Evidence | ATT&CK |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| exfil-archive (tar, dump) | `/tmp/.cache/dump.tar.gz` | T1560.001 |\r\n| exfil-endpoint (POST, exfil) | `/var/log/tomcat/access-exfil.log` | T1048 |\r\n\r\n## Persistence Mechanisms\r\n| Mechanism | Evidence | ATT&CK | Alerted |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| ssh-key-backdoor (ssh-ed25519, attacker) | `/root/.ssh/authorized_keys` | T1098.004 | **no** |\r\n| cron (curl, beacon) | `/var/spool/cron/tomcat` | T1053.003 | yes |\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\nHost confidentiality, integrity, and availability should be considered compromised until the\r\nremediation plan is executed and verified.\r\n\r\n## Attack Chain\r\nT1190 → T1505.003 → T1059.004 → {T1560.001, T1098.004, T1053.003, T1070.002}\r\n\r\n- T1190 → T1505.003\r\n- T1505.003 → T1059.004\r\n- T1059.004 → T1560.001\r\n- T1560.001 → T1048\r\n- T1059.004 → T1098.004\r\n- T1059.004 → T1053.003\r\n- T1059.004 → T1070.002\r\n# Vulnerability Report\r\n\r\nA CVE-driven entry vector was identified:\r\n\r\n- CVE-2023-50164 — `/opt/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/upload.jsp` (webshell (jsp, ognl))\r\n\r\nConfidence: high. Evidence cited inline.\r\n"]
[73.914047, "o", "# Baseline Report\r\n\r\nConfiguration and baseline weaknesses observed on the host:\r\n\r\n| Weakness | Evidence | Capability |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| vulnerable-lib (struts2, 2.5) | `/opt/tomcat/lib/struts2-core.jar` | BAS-01 |\r\n"]
[73.914474, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[73.914536, "o", "root@69151b65274e:/app/task# "]
[88.760916, "i", "grep -A 30 \"def _grounding\" /app/task/tests/criteria.py\n"]
[88.761341, "o", "grep -A 30 \"def _grounding\" /app/task/tests/criteria.py\r\n"]
[88.761374, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[88.76217, "o", "def _grounding(workspace: Path):"]
[88.762277, "o", "\r\n    \"\"\"Return a classifier path -> {'resolved','plausible','fabricated'} so every criterion"]
[88.762333, "o", "\r\n    shares one filesystem view of the evidence mounts (doc 02 §2.3).\"\"\"\r\n\r\n    def classify(path: str) -> str:\r\n        cands = _candidates(path)\r\n        if any(c.exists() for c in cands):\r\n            return \"resolved\"\r\n        if any(c.parent.exists() for c in cands):\r\n            return \"plausible\"          # wrong file/line inside a real directory\r\n        return \"fabricated\"             # parent directory absent under every mount"]
[88.762689, "o", "\r\n\r\n    return classify\r\n\r\n\r\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n# Framework-agnostic helpers (pure Python; no rewardkit dependency). Imported by the tier\r\n# files. The docs (doc 02/04) leave these as `_helpers`; here they are implemented in full.\r\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\ndef _haystack(finding: dict) -> str:\r\n    \"\"\"All searchable text of a finding: its claim plus its cited path strings.\"\"\"\r\n    return finding[\"claim\"] + \" \" + \" \".join(c[0] for c in finding[\"citations\"])\r\n\r\n\r\ndef _needles(artifact: dict) -> list:\r\n    \"\"\"Locator needles for finding an artifact's plan block: its path, the path basename, and\r\n    any `match` terms. Used by coverage's block lookup (within-plan, low collision risk).\"\"\"\r\n    path = artifact.get(\"path\", \"\")\r\n    base = path.rstrip(\"/\").split(\"/\")[-1] if path else \"\"\r\n    return [n for n in ([path, base] + list(artifact.get(\"match\") or [])) if n]\r\n"]
[88.762725, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@69151b65274e:/app/task# "]
[95.449131, "i", "grep -A 20 \"def _candidates\" /app/task/tests/criteria.py\n"]
[95.449674, "o", "grep -A 20 \"def _candidates\" /app/task/tests/criteria.py\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[95.450175, "o", "def _candidates(path: str) -> list:"]
[95.450218, "o", "\r\n"]
[95.450252, "o", "    \"\"\"Real filesystem candidate(s) a citation could resolve to, by mount prefix.\"\"\""]
[95.450323, "o", "\r\n    p = \"/\" + path.lstrip(\"/\")\r\n    for prefix, root in EVIDENCE_MOUNTS.items():\r\n        if p == prefix or p.startswith(prefix + \"/\"):\r\n            return [root / p[len(prefix):].lstrip(\"/\")]\r\n    # No mount prefix -> a host path inside the forensic image.\r\n    return [EVIDENCE_MOUNTS[HOST_ROOT] / p.lstrip(\"/\")]"]
[95.450415, "o", "\r\n\r\n\r\n@criterion(shared=True)\r\ndef _grounding(workspace: Path):\r\n    \"\"\"Return a classifier path -> {'resolved','plausible','fabricated'} so every criterion\r\n    shares one filesystem view of the evidence mounts (doc 02 §2.3).\"\"\"\r\n"]
[95.45047, "o", "\r\n    def classify(path: str) -> str:\r\n        cands = _candidates(path)\r\n"]
[95.450558, "o", "        if any(c.exists() for c in cands):\r\n            return \"resolved\"\r\n        if any(c.parent.exists() for c in cands):\r\n            return \"plausible\"          # wrong file/line inside a real directory"]
[95.450617, "o", "\r\n"]
[95.450728, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
